hilbertSequence(Module) -- compute the Hilbert sequence of a given module over an exterior algebra
**************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertSequence: (ExteriorIdeals)hilbertSequence,
  * Usage: 
        hilbertSequence M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a module over an exterior
        algebra E
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, nonnegative integers representing
        the Hilbert sequence of the quotient F/M

Description
===========

Let $\{g_1,g_2,\ldots,g_r\}$ be a graded basis of F with $deg(g_i)=f_i,\ i=1,
\ldots, r.$ Given $\sum_{i=f_1}^{n+f_r}{h_i t^i}$ the Hilbert series of a
graded E-module $F/M$, the sequence $(h_{f_1},\ldots,h_{n+f_r})$ is called the
Hilbert sequence of $F/M.$

Example:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : E = QQ[e_1..e_4, SkewCommutative => true]                               |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = E                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 4 skew commutative variable(s)                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M=image matrix {{e_1*e_2,e_3*e_4,0,0,0},{0,0,e_1*e_2,e_2*e_3*e_4,0},{0,0|
|                                                                             |
|o2 = image | e_1e_2 e_3e_4 0      0         0         |                      |
|           | 0      0      e_1e_2 e_2e_3e_4 0         |                      |
|           | 0      0      0      0         e_2e_3e_4 |                      |
|                                                                             |
|                             3                                               |
|o2 : E-module, submodule of E                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|,0,0,e_2*e_3*e_4}}                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : hilbertSequence M                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {3, 12, 15, 4, 0}                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

