isAlmostLexModule -- whether a monomial module over an exterior algebra is almost lex
*************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isAlmostLexModule M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a monomial module over an exterior algebra
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the module M is
        almost lex

Description
===========

Let $\{g_1,g_2,\ldots,g_r\}$ be a graded basis of F. A monomial submodule
$M=\oplus_{i=1} ^{r}{I_ig_i}$ of F is almost lex if $I_i$ is a lex ideal of E
for each $i.$

Example:

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : E = QQ[e_1..e_4, SkewCommutative => true]     |
|                                                   |
|o1 = E                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 4 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F=E^{0,0}                                     |
|                                                   |
|      2                                            |
|o2 = E                                             |
|                                                   |
|o2 : E-module, free                                |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I_1=ideal(e_1*e_2,e_1*e_3)                    |
|                                                   |
|o3 = ideal (e e , e e )                            |
|             1 2   1 3                             |
|                                                   |
|o3 : Ideal of E                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I_2=ideal(e_1*e_2,e_1*e_3,e_2*e_3)            |
|                                                   |
|o4 = ideal (e e , e e , e e )                      |
|             1 2   1 3   2 3                       |
|                                                   |
|o4 : Ideal of E                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : M=createModule({I_1,I_2},F)                   |
|                                                   |
|o5 = image | e_1e_3 e_1e_2 0      0      0      |  |
|           | 0      0      e_2e_3 e_1e_3 e_1e_2 |  |
|                                                   |
|                             2                     |
|o5 : E-module, submodule of E                      |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isAlmostLexModule M                           |
|                                                   |
|o6 = false                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : I_3=ideal(e_1*e_2,e_1*e_3, e_1*e_4)           |
|                                                   |
|o7 = ideal (e e , e e , e e )                      |
|             1 2   1 3   1 4                       |
|                                                   |
|o7 : Ideal of E                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isAlmostLexModule createModule({I_1,I_3},F)   |
|                                                   |
|o8 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note almostLexModule: almostLexModule, -- compute an almost lex module
    with the same Hilbert sequence of the module in input

